---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>32:18 Research</h1>
			<p>
				America is the wealthiest nation on earth, yet that wealth increasingly benefits a shrinking
				share of its people. Housing sits at the center of this shift: for many, it has stopped
				functioning as shelter and started functioning as an investment vehicle.
			</p>
			<p>
				32:18 exists to test that concern with data, not argument. Each piece here starts with a
				thesis, pulls public data, cleans it, and lays out the results, graphs, numbers, whatever
				the data shows. Source data is published alongside every piece so anyone can reproduce the
				analysis or take it in a different direction.
			</p>
			<p>Current lines of research:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Age of first-time and overall homebuyers, and what the gap reveals about generational wealth</li>
				<li>Tax allocation and its relationship to housing outcomes</li>
				<li>Car-centric infrastructure and transportation policy</li>
				<li>Energy programs and their downstream effects on cost of living</li>
				<li>Hyperurbanization: rural decline and its pressure on urban housing and wages</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Read the <a href="about/">About</a> page for more on the thinking behind this project, or
				browse the <a href="blog/">research</a> directly.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>